ORIGINAL WORK

All original work in this project is All Rights Reserved. You may not copy,
redistribute, modify, sublicense, or create derivative works from it without
prior written permission. This covers:

  - qol_compendium/          the mod itself, all Lua, scripts and assets
                             authored for it, including the moodle overlay
                             textures
  - tests/                   the headless test harness and its specs
  - tools/                   asset generators
  - included-mods.txt        and other project documentation


THIRD PARTY WORK

This project incorporates or adapts work from other Project Zomboid mods. That
work remains the property of its respective authors. The All Rights Reserved
grant above does not extend to it, and nothing here claims rights over it.

Where a source mod stated terms, those terms govern. Where a source mod stated
no terms, no permission has been granted by its author and the incorporation
rests on nothing more than the absence of an objection.

Status of each incorporated work, as recorded at time of integration:

  Immersive Overlays
    Workshop 533622988, by Stephanus van Zyl (Viceroy)
    Stated terms: none.
    Used: concept and blend behaviour. The five overlay textures are original,
    generated procedurally by tools/generate_overlays.py, and share no pixels
    with the source mod.

  Bigger Character Avatar
    Workshop 3245854570
    Stated terms: none.
    Used: concept only. The implementation here was written from scratch
    against the current build and shares no code with the original.

  Welding Torch Capacity
    Workshop 3044705007
    Stated terms: none.
    Used: concept only. The refill implementation here follows the base game's
    own algorithm, not the original mod's, and uses different values.

Mods whose authors explicitly prohibit redistribution, including inclusion in
another mod, are excluded from this project entirely and are recorded as
NO REDISTRIBUTE in included-mods.txt.


BASE GAME

Project Zomboid is the property of The Indie Stone. This project is an
unofficial modification, is not affiliated with or endorsed by The Indie Stone,
and is subject to their terms for user created content. Portions of this
project interoperate with, and follow the behaviour of, the base game's own
code and data.


CONTACT

For permission requests, or for any author who wishes their work removed from
